WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.133 --> 00:00:01.090
(upbeat music)

00:00:01.090 --> 00:00:03.270
- To stay ahead of the
field, Ford Performance

00:00:03.270 --> 00:00:05.320
constantly develop their race cars.

00:00:05.320 --> 00:00:08.090
Driver biometrics are
monitored second by second

00:00:08.090 --> 00:00:10.340
ensuring peak physical performance.

00:00:10.340 --> 00:00:11.780
Their next daring maneuver,

00:00:11.780 --> 00:00:13.743
harnessing the power of the mind.

00:00:16.540 --> 00:00:18.900
Ford are developing a
unique motorsport helmet

00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:21.150
that reads the drivers brain activity.

00:00:21.150 --> 00:00:23.650
Their team of engineers and
scientists have integrated

00:00:23.650 --> 00:00:26.400
cutting edge technology
electroencephalography,

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:30.100
or EEG for short, into the helmet itself.

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:32.800
EEG uses electrodes to
record electrical charges

00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:34.747
that signal activity in the brain.

00:00:34.747 --> 00:00:37.260
The team can measure driver
focus in high pressure

00:00:37.260 --> 00:00:39.270
situations to reveal crucial moments

00:00:39.270 --> 00:00:40.993
of suboptimal performance.

00:00:41.960 --> 00:00:45.060
The EEG electrodes lie within
the foam inside the helmet,

00:00:45.060 --> 00:00:46.970
in contact with the scalp.

00:00:46.970 --> 00:00:49.912
The brain data is then fed
out to external hardware.

00:00:49.912 --> 00:00:51.520
Drivers gain insight into

00:00:51.520 --> 00:00:53.460
how their brain performs while driving.

00:00:53.460 --> 00:00:56.010
This unique, bespoke
information can improve

00:00:56.010 --> 00:00:59.363
how they drive and in some
way, help them to win.

